Ours.  The RTG layer made card-neutral: the ZZ9000/Z3660 driver sits
behind the card record of patch 29, and nothing outside rtg/zz9000/ names
the card.  The same drawing as before on the ZZ9000/Z3660.

- rtg/rtgscreen.c (was zz9000/zz9000screen.c): the screen on cfb16, the
  GC wrapper and the colormaps; the visual from the card's caps;
- rtg/rtgdraw.c (from zz9000/zz9000draw.c): the run helpers, the CPU fill
  and copy (rtgCpuFill, rtgCpuCopy; the fill's stride is the mapped pitch,
  as the copy's always was, not the mode's width), the box order of a
  region copy, the direct PutImage, -blitmin (rtgBlitMin: the card's
  default unless given) and -move16 (rtgMove16); the blitter only through
  rtgCard, a flush with nothing queued one compare;
- rtg/zz9000/: the device, the mode, the map and the ZZ9KIOC_BLITS queue
  behind zz9000CardOps; its monitor switch the layer's int ioctl, exactly
  what the server always sent the zz9000 driver;
- rtg/rtgcards.c: the card table (RTG_ZZ9000), in -card auto's order;
- rtgInit.c takes the card once: -card NAME, else the card the server's
  name says (Xzz9000: zz9000), else (-card auto, or a name such as Xrtg or
  X) the first whose probe succeeds; a -mode is checked against the card's
  modes when the card is known, else once it is found; a -card this
  server has no driver for stops it with the list of its cards; the
  card's caps are read when it is taken and again after its initHW (no
  blitter: everything on the CPU; RTG_CAP_NOMOVE16: -move16 ignored);
- amixIo.c: -card; -blitmin, -move16 and -mode through the layer;
- the server is built under one name, AmixServerName (amix.cf; the
  package's host.def sets it), not Xzz9000.
MIT; the files' headers name their holders as before.

